# Integration Operations for Testing
# Guest Checkout Inventory Reservation System
#
# These operations require external dependencies (Redis, Sanity, time, etc.)
# and are not suitable for pure unit testing

## 1. State Machine Logic
### Token State Management
- [ ] Cache successful responses for 24 hours with TTL [INTEGRATION ONLY - Requires Redis/cache store]
- [ ] Return cached response on duplicate keys [INTEGRATION ONLY - Requires cache store]

## 2. Priority Processing Logic
### Queue Routing
- [ ] Queue processor checks priority queue first each cycle [INTEGRATION ONLY - Requires queue system]

## 3. Circuit Breaker Logic
### Failure Tracking
- [ ] Allow one test request after 30s cooldown to determine state [INTEGRATION ONLY - Requires time/system clock]

## 4. Timeout Logic
### TTL Management
- [ ] 10-minute TTL on reservation tokens [INTEGRATION ONLY - Requires Redis TTL, PRD lines 76, 84]
- [ ] Automatic rollback on timeout [INTEGRATION ONLY - Requires system triggers]

## 5. Core Queue Operations
### Queue Management
- [ ] Get queue lengths (BullMQ queue.getWaiting()) [INTEGRATION ONLY - Requires queue connection]

## 6. Request Validation Logic
### Input Verification
- [ ] Check if reservation token state is not FREE [INTEGRATION ONLY - Requires shared state]

# SUMMARY:
# Total integration operations: 7
# Require Redis: 3
# Require queue system: 2
# Require time/system clock: 1
# Require shared state: 1
